ountry>JP</country></address></addressbook> </applicant> <applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>IWAMOTO TAKEHIRO</name> <address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>OSHIMA MASANOBU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TAKASHIGE MASAO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>IDEMITSU PETROCHEMICAL CO., LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>IWAMOTO, TAKEHIRO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OSHIMA, MASANOBU</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAKASHIGE, MASAO</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>IWAMOTO TAKEHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>OSHIMA MASANOBU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TAKASHIGE MASAO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>IWAMOTO, TAKEHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OSHIMA, MASANOBU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAKASHIGE, MASAO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A self-supporting and easy open bag (11) having excellent easy opening capability and self-supportability, which comprises (a) a film containing L-LDPE as a main component, (b) a film made by biaxially stretching a raw film containing Ny6 as a main component at a stretch ratio of more than 2.8 in both MD and TD directions and (c) a biaxially stretched PET film, and has a main body thereof (12) manufactured by laminating the film (a) as a sealant layer (12A), the film (b) as an intermediate layer (12B) and the film (c) as a most external layer (12C) and, laminated along a tearing portion of the main body (12), a resin film for a tearing guide (13) having a directional arrangement of crystalline regions and a cut portion for tearing (15) formed in connection with the resin film for a tearing guide (13) and the main body (12).</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un sac (11) autoporteur particulièrement facile à ouvrir. Ledit sac comprend (a) un film renfermant un polyéthylène basse densité comme composant principal, (b) un film obtenu par étirement biaxial d'un film brut renfermant Ny6 comme composant principal, selon un taux d'étirement supérieur à 2,8 dans les directions MD et TD, et (c) un film PET étiré biaxialement. Le corps principal (12) du sac est fabriqué par stratification du film (a) comme couche (12A) de fermeture, du film (b) comme couche (12B) intermédiaire, et du film (c) comme couche (12C) extérieure. Le sac comprend également, stratifié le long d'une partie de déchirement du corps principal (12), un film en résine destiné à servir de guide (13) de déchirement et à structure directionnelle de régions cristallines, et une partie découpée de déchirement (15) formée conjointement avec le film de résine destiné à servir de guide (13) de déchirement et le corps principal (12).</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>